{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_templates",
  "description": "Expression-template library for the CISM-specific pointwise laws of the stage-2 CISM components (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00.002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch). Carries the pieces of the CISM basal traction, flow-factor, cap-coupling and vertical-grid physics that have no PISM/EqIce counterpart and are therefore not in the EqIce template libraries: (a) the bed-elevation friction-angle ramp of the PSEUDO_PLASTIC_OLD basal law (glissade_basal_traction.F90:256-277): phi = phimin below bedmin, phi = phimax above bedmax, and a linear ramp phi = phimin + (bed - bedmin)/(bedmax - bedmin) * (phimax - phimin) in between (the glide_types defaults are pseudo_plastic_phimin = 5 deg, pseudo_plastic_phimax = 40 deg, pseudo_plastic_bedmin = -300 m, pseudo_plastic_bedmax = 700 m, glide_types.F90:2380-2383), (b) the pressure-corrected temperature construction of the Paterson-Budd flow law (glissade_therm.F90:2596-2598): tempcor = clamp(temp - pmptemp, -50, 0) degC, where temp is the ice temperature and pmptemp the pressure melting point temperature in the same column (pmptemp = -rhoi*grav*pmlt*thck*stagsigma, glissade_therm.F90:2170), (c) the GLC cap import temperature transformation (drivers/cpl/nuopc/glc_import_export.F90:326-333): tsfc = ifelse(tsfc_raw - tkfrz < -250, 0, tsfc_raw - tkfrz) with the -250 degC sentinel clamp, and (d) the glide stretched-sigma vertical coordinate of glide_calc_sigma (libglide/glide_setup.F90:380-387): sigma(x, n) = (1 - (x+1)^(-n))/(1 - 2^(-n)) at the normalized level x = (up-1)/(upn-1) with the SIGMA_COMPUTE_GLIDE stretch exponent n = 2 (F90:303-308). The rest of the CISM basal and rheology physics is the same law as PISM's and is imported by reference from the EqIce libraries (../../eqice/stage2/basal_templates.esm: the Bueler & van Pelt / Tulaczyk effective pressure and the pseudo-plastic drag; ../../eqice/stage2/ice_rheology_templates.esm: the Paterson-Budd softness) with the CISM constants bound at the call sites. All templates here are match-less and invoked by name via apply_expression_template."
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "cism_phi_ramp": {
   "description": "Friction angle phi(bed) of the HO_BABC_PSEUDO_PLASTIC_OLD basal law (glissade_basal_traction.F90:256-277): phi = phimin where bed <= bedmin, phi = phimax where bed >= bedmax, and the linear ramp phi = phimin + (bed - bedmin)/(bedmax - bedmin) * (phimax - phimin) in between. bed is the bed elevation topg - eus [m] (with the CELL-CENTER topg, not stagtopg - the known quirk of this deprecated law, glissade_basal_traction.F90:261-263 and bugs.md #23, reproduced here); phimin/phimax are in degrees and bedmin/bedmax in m. CISM-specific: EqIce derives phi from data or inversion rather than from a bed-elevation ramp (CISM_LANE.md row 8).",
   "params": [
    "bed",
    "phimin",
    "phimax",
    "bedmin",
    "bedmax"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<=",
      "args": [
       "bed",
       "bedmin"
      ]
     },
     "phimin",
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
         "bed",
         "bedmax"
        ]
       },
       "phimax",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "phimin",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "bed",
               "bedmin"
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "bedmax",
               "bedmin"
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "phimax",
             "phimin"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_tempcor": {
   "description": "Pressure-corrected temperature of the FLWA_PATERSON_BUDD flow law (glissade_therm.F90:2596-2598): tempcor = min(0, temp - pmptemp), then tempcor = max(-50, tempcor) - i.e. clamp(temp - pmptemp, -50, 0) degC, with temp the ice temperature and pmptemp the pressure melting point temperature in the same layer (both degC, pmptemp <= 0). CISM-specific construction: PISM's Paterson-Budd law takes the pressure-adjusted absolute temperature directly; CISM clamps T - T_pmp to [-50, 0] degC before adding the 273.15 K offset (CISM_LANE.md row 4: 'small variant in the T* construction').",
   "params": [
    "temp",
    "pmptemp"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "max",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": -50.0,
      "units": "degC"
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "degC"
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "temp",
         "pmptemp"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_tsfc_import": {
   "description": "Cap import temperature transformation of the GLC NUOPC cap (drivers/cpl/nuopc/glc_import_export.F90:326-333): tsfc = ifelse(tsfc_raw - tkfrz < -250, 0, tsfc_raw - tkfrz), with tsfc_raw the mediator field Sl_tsrf [K] and tkfrz = SHR_CONST_TKFRZ = 273.15 K (glc_constants.F90:22-23, shr_const_mod.F90:37). The -250 threshold is applied to the CONVERTED value in degC (F90:333); the degC/K offset cancels in the comparison, so the condition is algebraically identical in K. The clamp is the 'Jer hack' sentinel (F90:328-332): land points where CLM sees ocean send a raw value of 0 K, which the -tkfrz conversion would drop to -273.15 degC; the clamp resets those to 0 degC. The subtraction is written twice because the template body has no let-binding (the Fortran converts and clamps in place on the same array). The mediator-to-model halo conversion (vector_to_spatial / parallel_convert_nonhaloed_to_haloed) is a grid operation and lives in the stage-3 assembly. CISM-specific: no PISM/EqIce counterpart (CISM_LANE.md row 15).",
   "params": [
    "tsfc_raw",
    "tkfrz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "tsfc_raw",
         "tkfrz"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": -250.0,
        "units": "degC"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "degC"
     },
     {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       "tsfc_raw",
       "tkfrz"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_sigma": {
   "description": "Glide stretched-sigma vertical coordinate sigma(x, n) = (1 - (x+1)^(-n))/(1 - 2^(-n)) of glide_calc_sigma (libglide/glide_setup.F90:380-387), evaluated at the normalized level x = (up-1)/(upn-1) with the SIGMA_COMPUTE_GLIDE stretch exponent n = 2 (F90:303-308): sigma(1) = 0 at the surface, sigma(upn) = 1 at the bed, and layer k occupies sigma(k)..sigma(k+1) with the thickness fraction sigma(k+1) - sigma(k). The reference run has upn = 11 layers, so the layer-1 interface is sigma2 = sigma(0.1, 2) = 0.23140495867768607 and the layer-10 interface is sigma10 = sigma(0.9, 2) = 0.96398891966759004; the cism_transport.esm MassBalance component applies the template at both levels (the layer thicknesses that the SMB accumulation/freeze-on tracer blends are scaled by). CISM-specific: PISM uses its own vertical grids (CISM_LANE.md rows 6/7), so the glide stretched-sigma formula has no EqIce counterpart.",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "n"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           "x",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "n"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 2.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "n"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}
